// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6632 new: Cloud Instance Metadata API Query for Credential Theft (T1552.005)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6632
// Pull request author: Gideon145
// Change: new rule
// Title: Cloud Instance Metadata API Query for Credential Theft
// Sigma ID: a1b3839d-705c-48b2-9d95-b773944bcdd9
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Gideon Opukeme
// Date: 2026-10-18 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552, T1552.005
// Description: Detects curl and wget querying a cloud instance metadata service for an endpoint that returns
//   temporary credentials or tokens for the role or managed identity attached to the instance.
//   Covers the AWS EC2 and ECS credential endpoints, the Azure managed identity token, and the GCP
//   service account token. Adversaries with code execution on a cloud workload query these link-
//   local endpoints to steal those credentials and move into the cloud control plane. The rule
//   matches only credential-bearing paths, so benign metadata lookups such as instance-id, region or
//   user-data do not fire. Scope is limited to curl and wget on purpose. Scripting-language clients
//   such as python, perl or nc are not covered here, since matching those images reliably would need
//   parent-process context the process_creation logsource does not provide.
// False positives:
//   - Cloud bootstrap or monitoring agents that read instance role credentials, filtered by parent process where the agent is known
//   - Administrators troubleshooting instance roles or managed identities
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1552.005/T1552.005.md
//   - https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/instance-metadata-security-credentials.html
//   - https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task-iam-roles.html
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/how-to-use-vm-token
//   - https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/access/authenticate-workloads
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/07a720664495912aae2565d3f19412205902ccf6/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_cloud_imds_credential_theft.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/curl" or FolderPath endswith "/wget") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "169.254.169.254" or ProcessCommandLine contains "169.254.170.2" or ProcessCommandLine contains "metadata.google.internal") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/meta-data/iam/security-credentials" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/v2/credentials" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/metadata/identity/oauth2/token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/computeMetadata/v1/instance/service-accounts") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/amazon-ssm-agent" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/ssm-agent-worker" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/google_guest_agent" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/google_metadata_script_runner" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/cloud-init")))
